Microsoft described a similar MFA swap in Storm-2949. The other four are the page's related defense topics.
notes:
One related kill chain on csoh.org, and the page's related defense topics.

At stage 05 the page links Storm-2949, where Microsoft described a similar MFA swap: existing methods removed and an attacker-controlled Microsoft Authenticator enrolled. There, Microsoft assessed with high confidence that the way in was abuse of self-service password reset. The page calls the swap similar and draws no other link between the two.

The four defense topics the page links are Azure security, IAM and cloud identity, incident response, and detection engineering. IAM stands for identity and access management.
